From df6ee10b9aeb8682a29e952bfc04649887363347 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:30:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: automatic disc changer, LoadExecPS2 handoff, crt0 argv,
 shared cards

A PC port has every disc up front, so the player never swaps discs:
- ps2_disc holds a disc set (--extra-disc). While the changer is armed (a
  game's disc-change scene calls PS2Runtime::armDiscChanger every frame), a
  lookup that misses on the current disc inserts the registered disc that
  has the file; open handles stay valid.
- The IOP's sceCdStatus reports a tray open/close cycle while armed, which
  is what the games' disc-change scenes wait for.
- PS2Runtime::loadExecPS2 re-executes the native binary registered for the
  requested program (--exec-target) with the same disc set (the disc holding
  the program boots), memory card root and arguments.
- SetupThread fills crt0's argument block (boot path + LoadExecPS2 args).
- --mc-root selects one memory card folder for the whole set.
- Disc images verified once are trusted later by file identity
  (~/.cache/ga2/disc-verify.json), so startup does not hash 19 GB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
